Subject: [PATCH 137/160] feat: Sandbox viewport: a built-in CineCam camera,
 Create Cinematic Camera, and the preview push

Editor side of decisions/s9-editor-cinecam-preview.md (LevelEditorViewport only).

- Camera menu: "CineCam" directly below "Default" - the same fly camera (IsDefaultCamera() stays
  true, navigation/FOV/cycling untouched) flagged as CineCam mode, which the cinematic camera
  plugin renders scene-referred with automatic adaptation. The choice persists through the
  personalization manager (module LevelEditorViewport, key CineCamCamera); the entity choice is
  not persisted, as stock.
- Per-frame push: right before SetViewCamera(m_Camera) in OnRender, in edit mode, the perspective
  viewport calls ICineCamEditorPreview::SetViewportPreview(mode, entityId, camera) - Entity for any
  camera entity it looks through (TrackView delegate cameras included), CineCam, or Default.
  The interface is resolved by name from CinematicCamera.dll (same pattern as CryPhoneTracker);
  without the plugin the viewport is exactly stock. ClearViewportPreview() on destruction and on
  level close / new level.
- "Create Cinematic Camera" below "Create Camera from Current View": the stock flow with the
  cinematic camera component GUID (it creates its own sibling camera component), FOV written
  through the sibling, the new entity selected, the viewport not switched. Stock item refactored
  into the shared CreateCameraFromCurrentView(); its behaviour is unchanged.

